From 1b5a0f853f9425c311e5d303c91bf879185724e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:46:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): origin-bound verified completions stay settled
 when the owner goes quiet [daveey]

Supersedes #3558, rebuilt on 6721503d602 (#3567), which fixed the replica
read for the same incident: workers 2, 5 and 7 were stopped on 2026-11-16 and
every card they had finished read as unreleased 450 s later (770 links).
This is what #3567 does not reach.

1. kanban_origin_ledger.project required a live, readable owner scope for
   every row, so an origin-bound (created) link to a verified completion on a
   quiet owner still projected unknown and superseded the released replica
   card. A verified completion that is still the owner's latest published
   record (same version, same data) is now settled: status, unfinished and
   stale no longer depend on the owner's heartbeat. Still required: a fresh
   origin pull, the stored released bit backed by verified evidence, a known
   status. A newer owner record reopens it. Open cards and unverified
   completions on a quiet owner stay unknown.
2. _ledger_links was last-copy-wins when two gateways publish the same card
   id. Now that a quiet owner's finished copy stays released for good, it
   could release the chat's one link to a copy still open elsewhere, so an
   open copy keeps the link whatever the order.

Why not caught: three tests pinned the old ledger rule for a verified record.
They now state the new one and keep their unverified or open control:
- test_fresh_transport_cannot_refresh_an_offline_owner[True]
- test_activity_consumers_share_live_verified_release (last step)
- test_alias_merge_never_releases_unavailable_or_unverified_evidence[expired]
  (the verified case moved to its own test; expired now runs unverified)

Tests: 6 new in test_kanban_release_survives_owner_offline.py. Against
main's code, 3 of them and 3 of the restated tests fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
